mod:call_result_deref_receiver_slice;
// DEF-315 + DEF-316 + DEF-317 (1.6.1e, landing 166): THREE ROOTLESS SHAPES RESOLVED TO
// THE STORAGE THEY REACH. (1) DEF-315: a `Self->` method whose receiver is the BARE
// DEREFERENCE of a call-result pointer -- `(<-(raw ids(@h))).sset()` -- was neither of
// the shapes `acc_call`'s receiver branch asks (a pointer-typed place chain, a bare call
// result), so the method's summary write of `self.s` met nothing: 113 at both legs under
// a view of `h.s`, a lent arena replaced under its task. The implicit `@recv` is a write
// at the dereference of a call-result pointer, DEF-309's shape, and takes DEF-309's road
// (`check_written` -> `check_access_reported`'s root==0 block -> `rootless_deref_base` ->
// `check_pointer_targets`' call-result arm; rule A reads a PARAMETER root too, DEF-311,
// and a result with two pointees). (2) DEF-316: a slice reached BELOW the dereference of
// a call-result pointer -- `(<-(raw idsl(@t)))[0i64].o`, `(<-(raw idbs(@bs))).sl[0i64].o`,
// the element moved out, its address handed to a writer, a method on it -- was re-rooted
// at the POINTEE and never asked what the slice there views; the named path's slice
// dispatch (`escape_written_slice_base` -> `check_slice_targets`, DEF-297) runs for a
// rootless place now, the call-result pointer on the base's path resolved by rule A
// (`escape_slice_targets_through_pointer`) and the slice's own holder read from the
// pointee (`escape_slice_own_holder_rootless`). (3) DEF-317: a call-result slice handed
// out of a struct CARRIER's slice field -- `wsl(raw getsl(@b))`, the result bound to a
// local, the carrier nested, literal-only, reached through a call-result or a NAMED
// pointer or behind a pointer field -- borrows the carrier whole, a ref the slice reader
// counted as a run at the carrier's own root, where no view of the array is rooted;
// `escape_carrier_runs` reads the carrier's chain (`b.sl = p.arr[0i64...2i64]`) for the
// runs it holds, a pointer to the carrier followed one hop at a time. Each shape here
// compiled on landing 165's compiler and read freed memory at both legs
// (`wt/51a/.internal/probes/t166/`, 81 cells, `MEASURED_165.md`). BORROW-015 at the
// method, the write or the call (a view); BORROW-016 (a lend).
//
// THE TRANSPARENT KINDS (sites 25-33; management_6's guard of 2026-10-29 04:28:44): the readers that
// resolve a rootless slice or pointer step the operators that are a call's value on ONE path -- `raw f()`
// (`ExprRawUnwrapExpr`), `f() ?! E` (`ExprEmphaticUnwrapExpr`: the value in slot a, the trap code in
// slot b; NOT `ExprRelayExpr`, which is the `relay` keyword's node), `g() ??! E` (D-360's Optional
// twin), `relay f()`, `await f()`, a cast `=>` or `=>!` -- in `escape_first_pointer_inward` and the
// two walks of `escape_slice_own_holder_rootless`; `?|` and `??` are TWO values and are not stepped
// (no own holder: the closed direction). For each kind one hazard site on each road where it is
// spellable: a may-fail getter's result relayed (`?!`) on the pointer road (25) and the slice road
// (32), an async getter's awaited result on both roads (26, 33; `async` sites), a call result cast to
// its own type `=>` (27, 28) and `=>!` (29, 30), a wild call-result pointer cast `=>!` to a plain one
// (31). Each was SILENT on landing 165 (113 at both legs: `wt/51a/.internal/probes/t166/cells4/`,
// `res165/cells4_165.txt`). Sites 32 and 33 were refused on this landing's first build for the WRONG
// reason -- the carrier `b`'s own view, because the `?!` node's kind was not among the stepped ones and
// the own-holder walk found no holder -- and their no-view twins (controls 31, 32 of the program test)
// were refused with them; the fix names the kind in the three walks, and the refusal names `vw`'s view.
//
// Three sites are PARITY sites, refused because their by-name twins are: element 1
// written through the dereference under a view of element 0 (`t[1i64].o = …` is refused:
// a run is judged whole), a COPY of the carrier's slice written with no view live
// (`H2[]:s2 = b.sl; s2[0i64].o = …` is refused: the write meets the carrier's own view),
// and a slice field written through the dereference of a call-result struct pointer
// while a SECOND slice of the array is live (`bsp.sl[0i64].o = …` through a named pointer
// is refused). Controls carrying no code (clean -- `call_result_deref_receiver_slice_ok.npk`):
// a method writing a DISJOINT field, a method writing nothing, the view's block ended,
// another pointee, the write before the view; a write through the dereference with no
// view live, a slice of ANOTHER array, a READ through the dereference; a READING callee,
// the call-result slice handed to the writer with no view live, a carrier over another
// array; the lend twins; and the by-name no-view twins. Closed by OTHER rules, not sites
// here: a member or an index BELOW the dereference as a receiver (`(<-(raw idt(@t))).inner
// .sset()`) is `acc_place`'s whole-place check (DEF-309); a TERNARY of addresses
// dereferenced is BORROW-015 at its `@h` arm; the slice VALUE `<-(raw idsl(@t))` handed to
// a writer is DEF-301's; a range of the dereference then indexed is BORROW-012; the call-
// result slice indexed DIRECTLY is TYPE-024. A `Self->` method on a POINTER FIELD below the
// dereference (`(<-(raw idsp(@sp))).p.sset()`) is DEF-312's two-level family (landing 167).
error:E1;
fixed Duration:J2 = Duration{ ns: 2000000000i64 };
struct:H2 = { string:o; int64:k; };
impl:H2 = { func:hset = NIL(H2->:self) never fails { self.o = string_concat("x", "y"); pass NIL; }; };
struct:S = { string:s; int64:k; };
impl:S = {
    func:sset = NIL(S->:self) never fails { self.s = string_concat("x", "y"); pass NIL; };
    func:kset = NIL(S->:self) never fails { self.k = 7i64; pass NIL; };
    func:snoop = NIL(S->:self) never fails { if (self.s.len == 999i64) { pass NIL; } pass NIL; };
};
struct:BS = { H2[]:sl; int64:k; };
struct:O = { BS:b; int64:k; };
struct:P = { H2[2]:arr; };
struct:PB = { BS->:bp; int64:k; };
struct:W = { shared_arena<int64>:a; int32:k; };
impl:W = {
    func:rep = NIL(W->:self) never fails { self.a = shared_arena_make(4i64); pass NIL; };
    func:kset = NIL(W->:self) never fails { self.k = 7i32; pass NIL; };
};
struct:HA = { shared_arena<int64>:a; int64:k; };
struct:BA = { HA[]:sl; int64:k; };

func:ids = S->(S->:x) never fails { pass x; };
func:pick_s = S->(bool:c, S->:a, S->:b) never fails { if (c) { pass a; } pass b; };
func:idsl = H2[]->(H2[]->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:idbs = BS->(BS->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:getslf = H2[](BS->:q) { pass q.sl; };
func:idbsf = BS->(BS->:q) { pass q; };
func:getslo = H2[]?(BS->:q) never fails { pass q.sl; };
func:idbso = BS->?(BS->:q) never fails { pass q; };
async func:getslaw = H2[](BS->:q) { pass q.sl; };
async func:idbsaw = BS->(BS->:q) { pass q; };
func:idbsw = wild BS->(BS->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:getsl = H2[](BS->:q) never fails { pass q.sl; };
func:getsl2 = H2[](O->:q) never fails { pass q.b.sl; };
struct:C1 = { BS->:bp; int64:k; };
struct:C2 = { C1->:c1p; int64:k; };
struct:C3 = { C2->:c2p; int64:k; };
struct:C4 = { C3->:c3p; int64:k; };
func:getslc2 = H2[](C2->:q) never fails { pass q.c1p.bp.sl; };
func:getslc3 = H2[](C3->:q) never fails { pass q.c2p.c1p.bp.sl; };
func:getslc4 = H2[](C4->:q) never fails { pass q.c3p.c2p.c1p.bp.sl; };
func:wsl = NIL(H2[]:s) never fails { s[0i64].o = string_concat("x", "y"); pass NIL; };
func:wsl1 = NIL(H2[]:s) never fails { s[1i64].o = string_concat("x", "y"); pass NIL; };
func:rsl = NIL(H2[]:s) never fails { if (s[0i64].o.len == 999i64) { pass NIL; } pass NIL; };
func:wr = NIL(H2->:p) never fails { p.o = string_concat("x", "y"); pass NIL; };
func:idw = W->(W->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:idsla = HA[]->(HA[]->:q) never fails { pass q; };
func:getsla = HA[](BA->:q) never fails { pass q.sl; };
func:wsla = NIL(HA[]:s) never fails { s[0i64].a = shared_arena_make(4i64); pass NIL; };
thread async func:filler = NIL(shared_arena<int64>->:s) joins J2 {
    await sleep(raw duration_ms(10i64)) ?| NIL;
    Handle<int64>:h = s.alloc(424242i64);
    int64:v = s.get(h) ?! E1;
    if (v != 424242i64) { fail E1; }
    pass NIL;
};
// --- THE VIEW DOMAIN ------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. (DEF-315) a `Self->` method writing `self.s` on the explicit dereference of a call-result pointer, under a view of `h.s`
func:method_on_deref_call = NIL() never fails {
    S:h = S{ s: string_concat("a", "b"), k: 1i64 };
    fixed uint8[]:vw = string_bytes(h.s);
    drop (<-(raw ids(@h))).sset();
    discard(vw[0i64] => int32);
    pass NIL;
};

// 2. (DEF-315) the call result rooted at a pointer PARAMETER (`(<-(raw ids(p))).sset()`), under a view of `p.s` (rule A reads the parameter, DEF-311)
func:method_on_deref_call_param = NIL(S->:p) never fails {
    fixed uint8[]:vw = string_bytes(p.s);
    drop (<-(raw ids(p))).sset();
    discard(vw[0i64] => int32);
    pass NIL;
};

// 3. (DEF-315) the method on the dereference of a call result that may be either of TWO pointees (`pick_s(c, @h, @g)`), under a view of `h.s`
func:method_on_deref_two_targets = NIL() never fails {
    S:h = S{ s: string_concat("a", "b"), k: 1i64 };
    S:g = S{ s: string_concat("c", "d"), k: 2i64 };
    fixed uint8[]:vw = string_bytes(h.s);
    bool:c = (h.k == 1i64);
    drop (<-(raw pick_s(c, @h, @g))).sset();
    discard(vw[0i64] => int32);
    pass NIL;
};

// 4. (DEF-316) a slice element's FIELD written through the dereference of a call-result pointer to the slice local, under a view of the array
func:slice_elem_field_through_deref_call = NIL() never fails {
    H2[2]:arr = [H2{ o: string_concat("a", "b"), k: 1i64 }, H2{ o: string_concat("c", "d"), k: 2i64 }];
    H2[]:t = arr[0i64...2i64];
    fixed uint8[]:vw = string_bytes(arr[0i64].o);
    (<-(raw idsl(@t)))[0i64].o = string_concat("x", "y");
    discard(vw[0i64] => int32);
    pass NIL;
};

